1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,510
Seventeen thousand dollars.

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,210
According to the NRMA,

3
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:06,790
that's how much some electric car owners
on a novated lease could lose in tax

4
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:11,390
savings because of a change that
starts on the 1st of April 2027.

5
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:14,990
And that's just one of the changes
coming for Aussie EV drivers next year.

6
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:16,790
In July 2027,

7
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:20,050
New South Wales plans to start
charging electric car owners for every

8
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,370
kilometre they drive.

9
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:26,150
Also in 2027, a new luxury car tax
threshold is due for electric vehicles.

10
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:30,230
And the emissions rules that have been
pushing car makers to discount EVs get

11
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,430
a lot tougher.

12
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:33,330
Some of these changes will save you money.

13
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:34,450
Some will cost you.

14
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,910
And depending on when you buy,

15
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:38,430
which state you live in and
how you pay for your car,

16
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,510
the difference could be
thousands of dollars.

17
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:41,530
So in this video,

18
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:45,050
I'll go through every major change
coming for electric car buyers and owners

19
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:48,370
in Australia in 2027 what's confirmed,

20
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:49,670
what's still being decided,

21
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:52,790
and what it means if you're thinking
about buying an EV in the next few

22
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:53,530
months.

23
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:57,340
Stay with me, because the timing of
your purchase has never mattered more.

24
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,570
Let's start with the big one:
the Electric Car Discount.

25
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:04,170
Since 2022, electric cars
provided by an employer,

26
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:05,810
including through a novated lease,

27
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:09,410
have been exempt from fringe benefits
tax as long as they're under the luxury

28
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,550
car tax threshold for
fuel-efficient vehicles.

29
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:17,070
That threshold is currently $91,387.

30
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:21,310
If you've never used one, here's how
a novated lease works in simple terms.

31
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:25,110
It's an agreement between you, your
employer and a leasing company.

32
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,370
Your employer pays the
car's costs the lease,

33
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:30,150
and often running costs like insurance,

34
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:34,630
servicing and charging out of your
salary before income tax is taken out.

35
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:36,550
That lowers your taxable income.

36
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:39,310
Normally, that benefit
attracts fringe benefits tax,

37
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:40,910
which eats into the saving.

38
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:43,870
For eligible EVs, that tax has been zero.

39
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,170
For a lot of Australians,

40
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:47,730
this has been the single
biggest reason to buy an EV.

41
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:51,550
A novated lease lets you pay for
the car out of your pre-tax salary,

42
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:55,210
and with no fringe benefits tax
on top, the savings can be huge.

43
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:59,030
The National Automotive Leasing and
Salary Packaging Association's chief

44
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,810
executive, Rohan Martin,

45
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:05,070
has called it "Australia's most effective
demand-side lever for EV uptake."

46
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:07,010
But it's been expensive
for the government.

47
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:10,890
A statutory review found that "the
revenue costs of the Electric Car Discount

48
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:12,770
are increasing significantly",

49
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:16,190
and that "alternative policy approaches
may be more fiscally efficient and

50
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,610
equitable." And it's been popular.

51
00:02:18,660 --> 00:02:22,230
Leasing industry groups have pointed
to the discount as a major reason EV

52
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,110
sales took off,

53
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:26,770
especially among middle-income workers
who could suddenly afford a new car

54
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:29,130
they'd never have
considered paying cash for.

55
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:30,770
So in May 2026,

56
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:34,260
the government confirmed the discount
would be wound back in three stages.

57
00:02:35,162 --> 00:02:36,892
Here's exactly how it works.

58
00:02:36,942 --> 00:02:41,092
Stage one: until the 31st of
March 2027, nothing changes.

59
00:02:41,142 --> 00:02:46,032
EVs under the fuel-efficient luxury car
tax threshold keep the full exemption.

60
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:51,752
Stage two: from the 1st of April
2027 to the 31st of March 2029,

61
00:02:51,802 --> 00:02:56,182
the full exemption only applies
to EVs costing $75,000 or less.

62
00:02:56,232 --> 00:02:58,772
Electric cars above $75,000,

63
00:02:58,822 --> 00:03:01,292
but still under the
luxury car tax threshold,

64
00:03:01,342 --> 00:03:05,372
get a twenty-five per cent discount on
their fringe benefits tax instead of a

65
00:03:05,422 --> 00:03:06,192
full exemption.

66
00:03:06,242 --> 00:03:09,792
Stage three: from the 1st of April 2029,

67
00:03:09,842 --> 00:03:12,652
all eligible EVs get the
twenty-five per cent discount.

68
00:03:12,702 --> 00:03:14,312
The full exemption is gone.

69
00:03:14,362 --> 00:03:16,112
And there are two important details.

70
00:03:16,162 --> 00:03:18,492
First, existing leases are protected.

71
00:03:18,542 --> 00:03:21,712
If you're already in an eligible
novated lease before the change,

72
00:03:21,762 --> 00:03:22,912
you're grandfathered.

73
00:03:22,962 --> 00:03:24,812
What does "grandfathered"
mean in practice?

74
00:03:24,862 --> 00:03:28,172
It means the rules that applied when
your lease started keep applying for that

75
00:03:28,222 --> 00:03:28,912
lease.

76
00:03:28,962 --> 00:03:31,092
You don't suddenly lose the
exemption halfway through.

77
00:03:31,142 --> 00:03:35,652
But when that lease ends and you take
out a new one, the new rules will apply.

78
00:03:35,702 --> 00:03:40,472
Second, plug-in hybrids already lost
their exemption on the 1st of April 2025.

79
00:03:40,522 --> 00:03:43,052
So this is only about fully electric cars.

80
00:03:43,102 --> 00:03:47,117
The NRMA estimated that some novated
lease EV owners could lose more than

81
00:03:47,167 --> 00:03:50,232
seventeen thousand dollars in
tax savings under the changes.

82
00:03:50,282 --> 00:03:52,012
Your own number depends on your salary,

83
00:03:52,062 --> 00:03:55,352
the car's price, the lease length
and the kilometres you drive.

84
00:03:55,402 --> 00:03:58,812
The Electric Vehicle Council welcomed
the fact that the discount was extended

85
00:03:58,862 --> 00:04:00,212
rather than scrapped outright.

86
00:04:00,262 --> 00:04:03,012
Its chief executive, Julie Delvecchio,

87
00:04:03,062 --> 00:04:06,172
said it was "good news for everyday
Australians who are doing the sums on

88
00:04:06,222 --> 00:04:07,142
going electric."

89
00:04:07,944 --> 00:04:09,594
So what does this mean for you?

90
00:04:09,644 --> 00:04:12,554
If you're looking at an EV under $75,000,

91
00:04:12,604 --> 00:04:17,974
the change on the 1st of April 2027
doesn't affect you at least until 2029.

92
00:04:18,024 --> 00:04:20,354
That covers a huge
chunk of the market now.

93
00:04:20,404 --> 00:04:22,314
In February 2026,

94
00:04:22,364 --> 00:04:25,882
CarsGuide listed seven electric cars
available for under forty thousand

95
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:28,534
dollars drive-away,
including the BYD Dolphin,

96
00:04:28,584 --> 00:04:34,794
the MG4, the GWM Ora, the Chery E5, the
Leapmotor B10 and the Hyundai Inster.

97
00:04:34,844 --> 00:04:41,054
And the BYD Atto 1 started from
$23,990 before on-road costs.

98
00:04:41,104 --> 00:04:44,994
But if you're looking at an EV
between $75,000 and the luxury car tax

99
00:04:45,044 --> 00:04:49,874
threshold think larger SUVs and
premium models the date matters a lot.

100
00:04:49,924 --> 00:04:53,714
Sign an eligible novated lease
before the 1st of April 2027,

101
00:04:53,764 --> 00:04:55,494
and you lock in the full exemption.

102
00:04:55,544 --> 00:04:58,954
Sign after, and you only get the
twenty-five per cent discount.

103
00:04:59,004 --> 00:05:02,914
That's why I'd expect a rush of more
expensive EV leases in the first three

104
00:05:02,964 --> 00:05:04,734
months of 2027.

105
00:05:04,784 --> 00:05:08,014
And it's why you should talk to your
employer and your lease provider now,

106
00:05:08,064 --> 00:05:11,834
rather than in March, when everyone
else is trying to do the same thing.

107
00:05:11,884 --> 00:05:13,554
One warning: delivery times.

108
00:05:13,604 --> 00:05:17,494
A lease generally needs the car to
actually be provided to you for the benefit

109
00:05:17,544 --> 00:05:21,234
to apply, so check with your
provider how the timing works.

110
00:05:21,284 --> 00:05:25,484
If the car you want has a long wait,
ordering in late March might be too late.

111
00:05:26,247 --> 00:05:29,017
Now, the second change:
the luxury car tax.

112
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:32,777
Right now, cars over a certain price pay
an extra tax of thirty-three per cent

113
00:05:32,827 --> 00:05:35,037
on every dollar above the threshold.

114
00:05:35,087 --> 00:05:37,937
For fuel-efficient vehicles,
including electric cars,

115
00:05:37,987 --> 00:05:41,897
that threshold is $91,387.

116
00:05:41,947 --> 00:05:44,677
On the 24th of March 2026,

117
00:05:44,727 --> 00:05:47,957
Prime Minister Anthony Albanese announced
a free trade deal with the European

118
00:05:48,007 --> 00:05:48,837
Union.

119
00:05:48,887 --> 00:05:49,797
As part of it,

120
00:05:49,847 --> 00:05:53,217
Australia agreed to remove the five
per cent tariff on European passenger

121
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:54,037
cars.

122
00:05:54,087 --> 00:05:58,297
And CarExpert reported a new luxury
car tax category for zero-emissions

123
00:05:58,347 --> 00:06:01,797
vehicles, with a threshold of $120,000.

124
00:06:01,847 --> 00:06:03,377
According to CarExpert,

125
00:06:03,427 --> 00:06:08,357
that new zero-emissions threshold is
due to start on the 1st of July 2027.

126
00:06:08,407 --> 00:06:10,977
The trade deal still needs
to be formally ratified.

127
00:06:11,027 --> 00:06:12,877
What does that mean in dollars?

128
00:06:12,927 --> 00:06:14,537
Here's a simple illustration.

129
00:06:14,587 --> 00:06:20,417
Today, an EV priced at $100,000
is $8,613 over the threshold.

130
00:06:20,467 --> 00:06:26,417
At thirty-three per cent, that's
about $2,842 in luxury car tax.

131
00:06:26,467 --> 00:06:31,417
Under a $120,000 threshold, the same
car would pay no luxury car tax at all.

132
00:06:31,467 --> 00:06:33,197
But don't get too excited.

133
00:06:33,247 --> 00:06:36,277
James Voortman, chief executive of
the Australian Automotive Dealer

134
00:06:36,327 --> 00:06:40,557
Association, welcomed the trade deal
but described the luxury car tax change

135
00:06:40,607 --> 00:06:44,157
as "a narrow change that will only
affect less than one per cent of vehicles

136
00:06:44,207 --> 00:06:48,277
sold." So this helps buyers
of premium EVs think Polestar,

137
00:06:48,327 --> 00:06:53,457
BMW, Mercedes-Benz, Porsche and Audi
much more than buyers of an everyday BYD

138
00:06:53,507 --> 00:06:54,387
or MG.

139
00:06:55,257 --> 00:06:58,427
Before we get to the change that could
affect every EV owner in New South

140
00:06:58,477 --> 00:07:00,327
Wales, a quick favour.

141
00:07:00,377 --> 00:07:03,387
Do you drive an EV, or are you
thinking about getting one?

142
00:07:03,437 --> 00:07:06,247
Would any of these 2027
changes make you buy sooner,

143
00:07:06,297 --> 00:07:07,987
or put you off completely?

144
00:07:08,037 --> 00:07:09,427
Tell me in the comments.

145
00:07:09,477 --> 00:07:10,337
And if you want honest,

146
00:07:10,387 --> 00:07:14,567
fact-checked videos about what's
changing for Aussie drivers in 2027,

147
00:07:14,617 --> 00:07:15,467
hit subscribe.

148
00:07:15,517 --> 00:07:16,517
It really helps.

149
00:07:17,337 --> 00:07:21,047
Now, the change that's causing the
biggest argument: paying per kilometre.

150
00:07:21,097 --> 00:07:24,827
Every time you fill up with petrol
or diesel, you pay fuel excise.

151
00:07:24,877 --> 00:07:28,907
That money goes to the federal budget,
and a large share is spent on roads.

152
00:07:28,957 --> 00:07:31,827
EV drivers don't buy fuel,
so they don't pay it.

153
00:07:31,877 --> 00:07:35,047
And fuel excise has been
in the spotlight in 2026.

154
00:07:35,097 --> 00:07:36,227
During the fuel crisis,

155
00:07:36,277 --> 00:07:38,487
the federal government
temporarily halved it,

156
00:07:38,537 --> 00:07:42,207
from 52.6 cents a litre to 26.3 cents,

157
00:07:42,257 --> 00:07:44,647
from the 1st of April
until the 1st of July.

158
00:07:44,697 --> 00:07:49,582
The NRMA also noted that the share of
fuel excise reinvested in roads fell to

159
00:07:49,632 --> 00:07:52,167
seventy per cent in the 2026 budget,

160
00:07:52,217 --> 00:07:55,367
down from seventy-nine per
cent forecast a year earlier.

161
00:07:55,417 --> 00:07:58,707
So the question of who pays for
roads is only getting bigger.

162
00:07:58,757 --> 00:08:02,947
Chasing Cars estimated that EVs cost
the federal government roughly $130

163
00:08:02,997 --> 00:08:08,087
million to $165 million a
year in lost fuel excise.

164
00:08:08,137 --> 00:08:12,287
New South Wales plans to fix that with
a road user charge from July 2027.

165
00:08:12,337 --> 00:08:17,447
Chasing Cars reported the proposed
rates as about 2.974 cents per kilometre

166
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:22,747
for electric vehicles and 2.379 cents
per kilometre for plug-in hybrids.

167
00:08:22,797 --> 00:08:27,727
AAP reported it was forecast to raise
$440 million in its first three years.

168
00:08:27,777 --> 00:08:29,067
What would that cost you?

169
00:08:29,117 --> 00:08:31,987
At 12,000 to 15,000 kilometres a year,

170
00:08:32,037 --> 00:08:37,887
Chasing Cars calculated an EV
driver would pay about $360 to $450.

171
00:08:37,937 --> 00:08:41,947
For comparison, a petrol car using seven
litres per hundred kilometres would

172
00:08:41,997 --> 00:08:48,467
pay around $440 to $550 a year in
fuel excise over the same distance.

173
00:08:48,517 --> 00:08:49,377
And notice something:

174
00:08:49,427 --> 00:08:51,827
plug-in hybrids would pay the charge too,

175
00:08:51,877 --> 00:08:55,467
even though they also burn petrol
and pay fuel excise when they do.

176
00:08:55,517 --> 00:08:58,467
That's one of the reasons critics
say the design needs work.

177
00:08:58,517 --> 00:09:00,127
But there's a legal problem.

178
00:09:00,177 --> 00:09:05,047
Victoria introduced a similar charge
2.8 cents per kilometre for EVs and in

179
00:09:05,097 --> 00:09:09,167
2023 the High Court found that only the
federal government can levy that kind

180
00:09:09,217 --> 00:09:10,307
of tax.

181
00:09:10,357 --> 00:09:12,207
So how can NSW go ahead?

182
00:09:12,257 --> 00:09:17,307
NSW Treasurer Daniel Mookhey has said
NSW would prefer a national system.

183
00:09:17,357 --> 00:09:19,967
But, quote, "in the absence
of a national system,

184
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:24,227
it remains the intent of the NSW
government to enact the law." He suggested

185
00:09:24,277 --> 00:09:28,607
the Commonwealth could refer its powers
to NSW to avoid another court defeat.

186
00:09:28,657 --> 00:09:33,257
As of mid-2026, NSW hadn't said
exactly how it would collect the money.

187
00:09:34,030 --> 00:09:35,940
And what about a national charge?

188
00:09:35,990 --> 00:09:40,660
In 2025, Treasurer Jim Chalmers said the
government was "accelerating work" on

189
00:09:40,710 --> 00:09:42,560
an EV road user charge.

190
00:09:42,610 --> 00:09:43,870
But in April 2026,

191
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:48,320
Transport Minister Catherine King told
the ABC she wasn't sure there was a

192
00:09:48,370 --> 00:09:50,220
path to pass one through parliament,

193
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:53,980
and that "it may not be the time for
it right now." The May 2026 federal

194
00:09:54,030 --> 00:09:55,840
budget didn't include one.

195
00:09:55,890 --> 00:09:59,460
The government said it was "continuing
to work with states and territories."

196
00:09:59,510 --> 00:10:00,980
So in 2027,

197
00:10:01,030 --> 00:10:04,400
you could end up with one state
charging EV drivers and the rest of the

198
00:10:04,450 --> 00:10:07,260
country not unless Canberra steps in.

199
00:10:07,310 --> 00:10:09,980
The reaction has been
strong on both sides.

200
00:10:10,030 --> 00:10:13,980
A NSW Government spokesperson argued
that "everybody who uses roads should

201
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:18,000
contribute to them." The NRMA and the
Electric Vehicle Council have both

202
00:10:18,050 --> 00:10:21,620
supported a road user charge in principle
but the Electric Vehicle Council

203
00:10:21,670 --> 00:10:25,540
argued it should only start once EVs
make up thirty per cent of the national

204
00:10:25,590 --> 00:10:26,360
fleet.

205
00:10:26,410 --> 00:10:28,800
Its chief executive, Julie Delvecchio,

206
00:10:28,850 --> 00:10:33,340
said the NSW tax "fails on all three
fronts." The council cited Sydney

207
00:10:33,390 --> 00:10:37,380
University research finding twenty-eight
per cent of likely EV buyers would be

208
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:39,720
dissuaded, and pointed to New Zealand,

209
00:10:39,770 --> 00:10:44,680
where it said the EV share of sales
fell from 20.6 per cent to 3.8 per cent

210
00:10:44,730 --> 00:10:46,440
after a similar move.

211
00:10:46,490 --> 00:10:50,460
Polestar Australia's boss Scott Maynard
called a national charge on EVs a

212
00:10:50,510 --> 00:10:54,220
"thinly veiled tax." It's worth
putting those numbers side by side.

213
00:10:54,270 --> 00:10:58,420
An average EV driver in NSW might pay
a few hundred dollars a year under the

214
00:10:58,470 --> 00:10:59,800
proposed charge.

215
00:10:59,850 --> 00:11:02,540
A petrol car doing the same
distance pays a similar amount,

216
00:11:02,590 --> 00:11:07,320
or more, in fuel excise plus the
much higher cost of the fuel itself.

217
00:11:07,370 --> 00:11:09,100
So even with a road user charge,

218
00:11:09,150 --> 00:11:13,380
running an EV on home charging is still
likely to be cheaper for most people.

219
00:11:13,430 --> 00:11:16,940
The question is whether the charge
arrives before EVs are affordable for

220
00:11:16,990 --> 00:11:17,780
everyone.

221
00:11:17,830 --> 00:11:18,640
My take?

222
00:11:18,690 --> 00:11:22,540
Some form of road user charge for EVs
looks very likely in the long run,

223
00:11:22,590 --> 00:11:26,260
because fuel excise is shrinking
as more people go electric.

224
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:28,240
The real fight is about when it starts,

225
00:11:28,290 --> 00:11:29,180
how much it is,

226
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:32,550
and whether it's fair compared with
what petrol and diesel drivers pay.

227
00:11:33,893 --> 00:11:37,655
Now, here's the change that could
actually make EVs cheaper in 2027:

228
00:11:37,705 --> 00:11:39,075
the emissions rules.

229
00:11:39,125 --> 00:11:41,135
Under the New Vehicle Efficiency Standard,

230
00:11:41,185 --> 00:11:45,535
the target for passenger cars drops
from 117 grams of carbon dioxide per

231
00:11:45,585 --> 00:11:49,895
kilometre in 2026 to 92 grams in 2027.

232
00:11:49,945 --> 00:11:52,815
That's a cut of more than twenty
per cent in a single year.

233
00:11:52,865 --> 00:11:57,455
Then 68 grams in 2028, and 58 in 2029.

234
00:11:57,505 --> 00:12:00,675
Car makers that miss their targets build
up penalties of roughly fifty dollars

235
00:12:00,725 --> 00:12:01,855
per gram per vehicle.

236
00:12:01,905 --> 00:12:06,455
The best way to avoid them is to
sell more electric and hybrid cars.

237
00:12:06,505 --> 00:12:09,855
And the fastest way to sell
more EVs is to cut prices.

238
00:12:09,905 --> 00:12:11,015
We've already seen it.

239
00:12:11,065 --> 00:12:17,875
Hyundai cut up to $13,857 from some
versions of the Kona Electric in 2026.

240
00:12:17,925 --> 00:12:21,195
And CarsGuide reported that the government's
Clean Energy Finance Corporation

241
00:12:21,245 --> 00:12:24,915
committed sixty million dollars to
Hyundai Capital Australia to help offer

242
00:12:24,965 --> 00:12:27,795
cheaper finance on Hyundai and Kia EVs.

243
00:12:27,845 --> 00:12:29,235
And it isn't just about price cuts.

244
00:12:29,285 --> 00:12:31,175
The tougher the targets get,

245
00:12:31,225 --> 00:12:34,915
the more EV and hybrid models car
makers need to bring to Australia.

246
00:12:34,965 --> 00:12:38,595
More than sixty new EV models were
expected to enter the Australian market as

247
00:12:38,645 --> 00:12:40,015
the scheme started.

248
00:12:40,065 --> 00:12:41,915
More choice usually
means more competition,

249
00:12:41,965 --> 00:12:45,115
and more competition
usually means better deals.

250
00:12:45,165 --> 00:12:47,035
The market is already moving fast.

251
00:12:47,085 --> 00:12:50,415
The Australian Automobile Association
reported that battery electric and

252
00:12:50,465 --> 00:12:55,635
plug-in hybrid vehicles made up 31.61
per cent of new light vehicle sales in

253
00:12:55,685 --> 00:12:57,275
the June quarter of 2026.

254
00:12:57,325 --> 00:12:59,795
By September 2026,

255
00:12:59,845 --> 00:13:03,555
battery electric cars made up more than
twenty-four per cent of new car sales.

256
00:13:03,605 --> 00:13:07,955
CarExpert reported that EVs outsold both
petrol and diesel vehicles in August

257
00:13:08,005 --> 00:13:10,135
and September 2026.

258
00:13:10,185 --> 00:13:11,955
And as we covered in our last video,

259
00:13:12,005 --> 00:13:16,255
the federal opposition has promised to
scrap the NVES if it wins government so

260
00:13:16,305 --> 00:13:18,495
this part of the picture could change too.

261
00:13:18,545 --> 00:13:22,075
And there's one more change from
the 2026 budget worth knowing about.

262
00:13:22,125 --> 00:13:25,708
The government committed forty million
dollars to new regional and kerbside

263
00:13:25,758 --> 00:13:26,095
chargers.

264
00:13:26,145 --> 00:13:29,955
That matters, because a lack of charging
is still one of the biggest reasons

265
00:13:30,005 --> 00:13:33,885
people give for not buying an EV,
especially outside the big cities.

266
00:13:34,725 --> 00:13:38,715
So, should you buy an
EV before 2027, or wait?

267
00:13:38,765 --> 00:13:40,295
Here's how I'd think about it.

268
00:13:40,345 --> 00:13:44,535
If you're buying an EV over
$75,000 through a novated lease:

269
00:13:44,585 --> 00:13:47,915
the deadline is the 31st of March 2027.

270
00:13:47,965 --> 00:13:49,595
Get your lease in place before then,

271
00:13:49,645 --> 00:13:52,415
and check how delivery timing
works with your provider.

272
00:13:52,465 --> 00:13:57,535
If you're buying a premium EV
between about $91,000 and $120,000,

273
00:13:57,585 --> 00:13:59,735
paying cash or with a normal loan:

274
00:13:59,785 --> 00:14:04,355
the new luxury car tax threshold
is due from the 1st of July 2027.

275
00:14:04,405 --> 00:14:08,015
Waiting could save you thousands but
only if the trade deal is ratified on

276
00:14:08,065 --> 00:14:08,465
time.

277
00:14:08,515 --> 00:14:12,535
Ask the dealer how they'll handle the
timing, and get any promise in writing.

278
00:14:12,585 --> 00:14:14,155
If you live in New South Wales:

279
00:14:14,205 --> 00:14:20,255
budget for a possible road user charge
from July 2027 roughly $360 to $450

280
00:14:20,305 --> 00:14:24,015
a year for an average driver,
based on the proposed rate.

281
00:14:24,065 --> 00:14:27,015
That's still less than the fuel
excise most petrol cars pay,

282
00:14:27,065 --> 00:14:28,455
but it's a new cost.

283
00:14:28,505 --> 00:14:29,615
If you're buying a cheaper EV,

284
00:14:29,665 --> 00:14:35,055
under $75,000: the fringe benefits tax
change doesn't affect you until 2029.

285
00:14:35,105 --> 00:14:38,415
And with tougher
emissions targets in 2027,

286
00:14:38,465 --> 00:14:41,285
there's a good chance car makers
will keep pushing EV discounts.

287
00:14:41,335 --> 00:14:45,235
Shop around, compare drive-away
prices, and don't rush.

288
00:14:45,285 --> 00:14:46,365
And think about resale.

289
00:14:46,415 --> 00:14:50,875
Rules that make new EVs cheaper or more
expensive can also move the value of

290
00:14:50,925 --> 00:14:51,755
used ones.

291
00:14:51,805 --> 00:14:55,775
If luxury car tax falls on
premium EVs from July 2027,

292
00:14:55,825 --> 00:14:59,675
for example, buyers may compare a used
premium EV with a cheaper new one.

293
00:14:59,725 --> 00:15:02,855
Nobody can predict exactly
how prices will move,

294
00:15:02,905 --> 00:15:05,275
so buy a car you're happy
to keep for a while.

295
00:15:05,325 --> 00:15:08,835
And whatever you do, don't let a
deadline push you into the wrong car.

296
00:15:08,885 --> 00:15:11,705
A tax saving doesn't help if
the car doesn't suit your life.

297
00:15:12,446 --> 00:15:16,776
So, here's 2027 for Aussie
EV drivers in a nutshell.

298
00:15:16,826 --> 00:15:18,226
On the 1st of April 2027,

299
00:15:18,276 --> 00:15:23,556
the full fringe benefits tax exemption
is limited to EVs costing $75,000 or

300
00:15:23,606 --> 00:15:24,116
less.

301
00:15:24,166 --> 00:15:27,536
Plug-in hybrids already
lost theirs in 2025.

302
00:15:27,586 --> 00:15:29,296
In July 2027,

303
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:32,796
NSW plans to start charging
EV drivers per kilometre,

304
00:15:32,846 --> 00:15:34,956
unless the federal government steps in.

305
00:15:35,006 --> 00:15:36,996
Also from July 2027,

306
00:15:37,046 --> 00:15:41,936
a new $120,000 luxury car tax threshold
is due for zero-emissions vehicles,

307
00:15:41,986 --> 00:15:44,696
if the European trade deal is ratified.

308
00:15:44,746 --> 00:15:48,816
And tougher emissions targets will keep
pushing car makers to sell more EVs

309
00:15:48,866 --> 00:15:50,456
which could mean more discounts.

310
00:15:50,506 --> 00:15:51,466
So, mark these dates.

311
00:15:51,516 --> 00:15:54,096
The 31st of March 2027:

312
00:15:54,146 --> 00:15:58,696
the last day for the full exemption
on EVs over $75,000 in a new novated

313
00:15:58,746 --> 00:15:59,536
lease.

314
00:15:59,586 --> 00:16:02,976
The 1st of April 2027:
the new rules start.

315
00:16:03,026 --> 00:16:05,176
The 1st of July 2027:

316
00:16:05,226 --> 00:16:09,356
the new luxury car tax threshold
for zero-emissions vehicles is due,

317
00:16:09,406 --> 00:16:11,876
and the NSW road user charge is planned.

318
00:16:11,926 --> 00:16:13,716
And through all of 2027:

319
00:16:13,766 --> 00:16:15,356
tougher emissions targets for car makers,

320
00:16:15,406 --> 00:16:17,616
and a government review of those rules.

321
00:16:17,666 --> 00:16:19,336
Some of these changes cost money.

322
00:16:19,386 --> 00:16:20,536
Some save money.

323
00:16:20,586 --> 00:16:23,416
All of them make timing
more important than ever.

324
00:16:23,466 --> 00:16:25,416
If this helped, hit like, subscribe,

325
00:16:25,466 --> 00:16:28,036
and share it with someone who's
thinking about going electric.

326
00:16:28,086 --> 00:16:29,116
Tell me in the comments:

327
00:16:29,166 --> 00:16:32,296
will these changes make you
buy an EV sooner, or later?

328
00:16:32,346 --> 00:16:33,216
And in the next video,

329
00:16:33,266 --> 00:16:37,516
we'll look at the new cars coming to
Australia in 2027 and which ones could

330
00:16:37,566 --> 00:16:38,856
shake up the market.

331
00:16:38,906 --> 00:16:39,706
See you there.
